──────────────────────────────── ATTACK SURFACE
───────────────────────────────────────
1. Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
   • Any XSS flaw anywhere in the application allows the attacker to
run:
   ```js
   const pk = localStorage.getItem("privateKeyModulePK");
   // exfiltrate pk via fetch or image beacon
   ```
2. Compromised dependency / analytics tag
   • Third-party script that the site trusts can simply read
localStorage
     and leak the key on page load.
3. Browser extensions
   • A malicious or compromised extension with `<all_urls>` permission
can
